TeX Live 2026 for RISC OS
=========================

This is a development version of a port of TeX Live 2026 to RISC OS 5,
for testing. It provides pdfTeX, with LaTeX, from the command line. There
is no desktop front end yet.

Project: https://github.com/kierennicolas/ArmTex_update


Installing
----------

1. Install SharedUnixLibrary 1.07 or later (PackMan has it).
2. Copy !TeXLive anywhere you like, for example to $.Apps.
3. Double-click !TeXLive once. It does not open a window: it makes the
   commands below available. After that, the Filer sets them up again
   whenever it sees !TeXLive (for example when you open the directory
   holding it).


Using it
--------

Press F12, or open a task window (Ctrl-F12), and go to the directory
holding your document:

    *Dir ADFS::HardDisc4.$.Documents

Then:

    *pdflatex mydoc

typesets mydoc/tex with LaTeX and writes mydoc/pdf, with mydoc/log and
mydoc/aux, in the same directory. Run it again if LaTeX asks you to (for
cross-references). Use pdftex instead of pdflatex for plain TeX.

TeX names files as Unix does: mydoc.tex on the command line is the RISC OS
file mydoc/tex.

Useful options:

    -interaction=nonstopmode   do not stop at errors to ask what to do
    -halt-on-error             stop at the first error

kpsewhich finds a file in the TeX tree, for example:

    *kpsewhich article.cls


Commands
--------

    pdflatex    LaTeX, writing PDF
    pdftex      plain TeX (with e-TeX), writing PDF
    kpsewhich   look up files and settings in the TeX tree


What is included
----------------

TeX Live's scheme-basic: plain TeX, LaTeX and the packages LaTeX needs,
with Computer Modern and the AMS fonts. Formats were made on the build
machine. More packages, engines (LuaLaTeX, DVI output) and a desktop front
end are planned.


